804 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 553 0 R
/E (Based on the research that we conducted, we discovered that there is a need to tread carefully in the way we approach the DHH community. It is important to communicate in a manner that is perceived as approachable. In order for the Red Cross to be an effective asset and partner with the community, they first need to establish a relationship to foster a sense of trust. Beyond that, the DHH community will also view the Red Cross as a safe, empowering, and dependable place to confide in. )
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
805 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 553 0 R
/E (Our activations will address our communication strategy by first introducing a collaboration between the Deaf Culture Alliance Social Club and the American Red Cross to build a stronger relationship with the DHH community before promoting resources. We want the DHH community to get comfortable with the American Red Cross and see the relationship as mutualistic.)
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
