<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 557 0 R
/E (Some places are focused on bridging the gap between Deaf people and hearing people. However, there are some places that are only a space for Deaf people to exist and maintain their culture and structure.)
/Pg 27 0 R
/K [12]
>>
endobj
911 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 557 0 R
/E (We concluded that  Deaf Artisan Market Day and Crepe Crazy have the lowest entry barrier as anyone can enjoy this without being a part of the community. FaceBook groups allow anyone to join or post and are open to outside resources so they are also a low entry barrier. )
/Pg 27 0 R
/K [13]
>>
endobj
912 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 557 0 R
/E (Then we have the Deaf Austin Theatre, The School for the Deaf and Austin Deaf Club which, based on our research, we decided these organizations have a high entry barrier because they are less open to outside resources, lack public information, are difficult to contact, and will likely need an inside referral to get in touch.)
/Pg 27 0 R
/K [14]
>>
endobj
