/E (The scene opens with darkness and silence, setting a tense atmosphere. Suddenly, a dog with its mouth open appears, its barking muffled, flashing on the screen momentarily. Darkness takes over once more, only to be interrupted by a flashing fire alarm with its beeping muffled. Silence and darkness return, then are cut through by the image of the dog, now barking with greater urgency, yet still muffled. This is scene alludes to someone coming in and out of sleep, getting only small pieces of information. )
/Pg 33 0 R
/K [4]
>>
