/E (The scene unfolds similar to the "Dog" spot,  in darkness and silence. Abruptly, a face materializes, articulating "wake up"  in a muffled voice. This brief plea is soon shrouded by darkness once again, which is swiftly cut by the urgent glow of a fire alarm's red light, its sound muffled. The darkness engulfs the scene again, only to be disrupted as the face re-emerges, mouthing "wake up" this time a louder, but still muffled. This echoes the earlier spot's theme of awakening, here featuring Jane as she tries to rouse Granny.)
/Pg 35 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
