<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 566 0 R
/E (The spot then moves to a bedroom where Granny, an elderly woman with hearing loss, sleeps, oblivious to the fire alarm and the danger it signals. Her granddaughter, Jane, works to awaken her, shaking Granny's bed and using sign language to stress the gravity of the situation. The essence of this narrative is the danger of depending solely on the sense of smell for fire detection, which is both perilous and ineffective. It informs the viewer about life-saving devices like bed shaker alarms, essential for those who cannot rely on conventional auditory alerts.)
/Pg 36 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
